            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8674-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8674 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Initializing the DNS stub resolver from an /etc/resolv.conf file, or a LOCALDOMAIN environment variable, whose search list contains a domain of roughly 200 characters or more in the GNU C Library version 2.26 to 2.44 results in an assertion failure which aborts the process.  The resolver truncates the search list when copying it into the fixed-size _res.defdname buffer, then asserts that the copy is consistent with the full configuration.  The consistency check compared against the wrong size and did not handle a first entry that does not fit, so a correctly truncated list failed the assertion.  Any process that resolves names through the library is affected, including long-running processes that reload /etc/resolv.conf on the next query after it changes.  Search domains are commonly written to /etc/resolv.conf from data received over DHCP or from a VPN server, so an attacker on the local network may be able to trigger this without privileges on the target system, subject to validation by the network configuration software."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8674",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8674\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.43-5\nFix Version: 2.43-6\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8674](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8674)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8674**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-bin  | 2.43-5  | 2.43-6  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8674](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8674)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libc-bin@2.43-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8674-libc-gconv-modules-extra",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8674 medium vulnerability for libc-gconv-modules-extra package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Initializing the DNS stub resolver from an /etc/resolv.conf file, or a LOCALDOMAIN environment variable, whose search list contains a domain of roughly 200 characters or more in the GNU C Library version 2.26 to 2.44 results in an assertion failure which aborts the process.  The resolver truncates the search list when copying it into the fixed-size _res.defdname buffer, then asserts that the copy is consistent with the full configuration.  The consistency check compared against the wrong size and did not handle a first entry that does not fit, so a correctly truncated list failed the assertion.  Any process that resolves names through the library is affected, including long-running processes that reload /etc/resolv.conf on the next query after it changes.  Search domains are commonly written to /etc/resolv.conf from data received over DHCP or from a VPN server, so an attacker on the local network may be able to trigger this without privileges on the target system, subject to validation by the network configuration software."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8674",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8674\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-gconv-modules-extra\nVersion: 2.43-5\nFix Version: 2.43-6\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8674](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8674)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8674**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libc-gconv-modules-extra  | 2.43-5  | 2.43-6  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8674](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8674)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libc-gconv-modules-extra@2.43-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
